    "id": "4aaabac2cead751c68b88774",
    "path": "tracing_subscriber::fmt::time::time_crate::OffsetTime",
    "name": "OffsetTime",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "tracing-subscriber",
    "version": "0.3.23",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct OffsetTime<F>",
    "docs": "Formats the current time using a fixed offset and a [formatter] from the [`time` crate].\n\nThis is typically used as an alternative to [`LocalTime`]. `LocalTime` determines the offset\nevery time it formats a message, which may be unsound or fail. With `OffsetTime`, the offset is\ndetermined once. This makes it possible to do so while the program is still single-threaded and\nhandle any errors. However, this also means the offset cannot change while the program is\nrunning (the offset will not change across DST changes).\n\n[formatter]: time::formatting::Formattable\n[`time` crate]: time",
